B.aj3=new A.hv("1. Acceptance of Terms",'By accessing, downloading, installing, registering an account on, or interacting with the ClassRealm mobile application, Progressive Web Application (PWA), or associated school web portals (collectively referred to as the "System"), you explicitly acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to be legally bound by these Terms of Service in conjunction with the ClassRealm Privacy Policy.\n\nClassRealm is an Integrated Senior High School Academic Management, Attendance Tracking, and Learning Portal engineered specifically for Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School. These Terms constitute a binding institutional agreement between all active end-users (Administrators, Teachers, Students, and Parents/Legal Guardians) and the educational administration. If you do not consent to, understand, or agree with any stipulation set forth in these Terms, you must immediately discontinue use of the System, uninstall the application from your devices, and notify your Class Adviser or School ICT Coordinator.')
B.ajl=new A.hv("2. Purpose, Institutional Scope, and Intended Use","ClassRealm is deployed strictly and exclusively for legitimate educational, classroom administration, academic performance evaluation, institutional communication, and campus security purposes within Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School.\n\nThe System supports four (4) distinct role-based access tiers:\n\u2022 School Administrator Portal: Enterprise-level management of school year terms, academic calendars, teacher onboarding, centralized emergency announcements, audit log inspection, and platform operational health.\n\u2022 Teacher Portal: Encoding, computing, and releasing official learner grades, managing classroom RFID/NFC attendance sessions, authoring digital assessments, publishing learning modules, and conducting live anti-cheating supervision.\n\u2022 Student Portal: Reviewing personalized class schedules, accessing learning materials, taking proctored assessments, monitoring attendance scan records, and tracking quarterly academic progress.\n\u2022 Parent and Guardian Portal: Read-only monitoring of their linked child's daily campus attendance, official announcements, teacher directory, and authorized academic grades.\n\nCommercial exploitation, external advertising, unauthorized third-party integrations, and any utilization outside sanctioned school operations are strictly prohibited.")
B.aj4=new A.hv("3. User Accounts, Access Credentials, and Role Responsibilities","Access to ClassRealm is restricted to verified members of the Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School community. All users are personally responsible for upholding the confidentiality of their credentials and adhering to their assigned roles:\n\n\u2022 System Administrators: Obligated to enforce institutional data protection standards, manage teacher access permissions, safeguard master database credentials, schedule non-disruptive maintenance windows, and ensure prompt response to data privacy inquiries.\n\u2022 Teachers: Must ensure prompt, objective, and accurate recording of attendance, learning outputs, and quarterly grades adhering strictly to Department of Education (DepEd) standards under the Strengthened Senior High School Curriculum (DepEd Order No. 15, s. 2026). Teachers must never share their master portal credentials or grant unverified individuals access to student records.\n\u2022 Students: Expected to demonstrate unwavering academic honesty during examinations, submit their own original classwork, maintain the security of their login credentials, and use only their personally issued RFID card for campus gate and classroom attendance.\n\u2022 Parents and Legal Guardians: Granted non-editable, read-only monitoring access to foster active parental guidance. Parents agree to utilize the portal solely for supporting their child's academic growth and must refrain from attempting to alter records, compromise other student accounts, or impersonate their child during online assessments.")
B.ajm=new A.hv("4. RFID Card Attendance, Scanner Hardware, and Anti-Proxy Regulations",'ClassRealm utilizes an integrated attendance architecture combining physical ESP32 RFID scanning terminals with optional teacher NFC verification devices:\n\n\u2022 Physical Card Possession: Every student is issued an individual school RFID card linked to their unique Learner Reference Number (LRN). The card remains the student\'s personal responsibility throughout the academic school year.\n\u2022 Tap Execution: Students must tap only their own card upon arriving at and departing from designated school scanning terminals. Tapping on behalf of an absent or late classmate ("proxy attendance") constitutes a severe breach of school discipline and will result in disciplinary action under the EBSIS Student Code of Conduct.\n\u2022 Hardware Tampering: Any attempt to physically damage, disconnect, tamper with, clone, emulate via unauthorized wireless transmitters, or manipulate classroom RFID readers or school network infrastructure is strictly prohibited and subject to immediate administrative sanctions and disciplinary review.')
B.aj7=new A.hv("5. Academic Integrity and Real-Time Anti-Cheating Proctoring Safeguards","To preserve academic credibility and fair assessment standards during digital quizzes, long tests, and quarterly examinations, ClassRealm deploys an automated real-time proctoring engine:\n\n\u2022 Telemetry and Anomaly Detection: During active assessment sessions, the System monitors and records application lifecycle state events. This includes detecting tab switches, browser focus loss, window minimization, split-screen multi-tasking, backgrounding the application, and unauthorized copy/paste attempts (\"suspicious session events\").\n\u2022 Proctor Alerts and Automated Enforcement: Detected anomalies are transmitted in real time to the proctoring teacher's monitoring console. Based on the frequency and severity of detected anomalies, the teacher or the System may automatically issue on-screen warnings, temporarily lock the assessment session, deduct score points, or terminate the student's exam attempt, requiring a formal supervised retake.\n\u2022 Privacy Guarantee: ClassRealm does NOT record camera feeds, microphone audio, screen video recordings, browser history outside the assessment page, personal photo files, or device GPS locations. The telemetry engine is operational strictly while an assessment attempt is in progress.")
B.ajc=new A.hv("6. Adult Student Grade Privacy Rights (18 Years Old and Above)","In strict compliance with the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173), students who have reached the age of majority (eighteen [18] years old and above) possess independent statutory privacy rights over their sensitive educational records:\n\n\u2022 Privacy Controls: Adult learners are provided with configurable \"Parent / Guardian Privacy Controls\" within their Student Settings screen, allowing them to enable or restrict parent/guardian visibility over their Quarterly Term Grades and Final Computed Grades.\n\u2022 Non-Restricted Safety Records: Daily campus attendance timestamps, emergency broadcast notifications, class schedules, and institutional announcements remain continuously accessible to linked parents/guardians regardless of the student's age, in accordance with the school's duty of care, campus safety policies, and institutional parental communication guidelines.")
B.aj5=new A.hv("7. Acceptable Use, System Security, and Prohibited Activities","Users must utilize ClassRealm in an ethical, lawful, and constructive manner. The following actions are strictly forbidden:\n\n\u2022 Credential Sharing: Disclosing, transferring, selling, or lending user passwords, One-Time Passwords (OTPs), or active session tokens to any other party.\n\u2022 Unauthorized Access: Attempting to bypass role-based security boundaries, intercept administrative endpoints, escalate user privileges, or view academic and personal records of unassigned students.\n\u2022 Malicious Uploads: Uploading files containing viruses, malicious scripts, corrupted executables, offensive media, or copyrighted materials without proper authorization.\n\u2022 Infrastructure Attacks: Launching Denial-of-Service (DoS) attacks, brute-force password cracking, reverse-engineering local Drift/SQLite schemas, or probing cloud endpoints with automated vulnerability scanners.\n\nTo protect institutional data integrity, ClassRealm implements progressive automated rate-limiting, temporary IP and device lockouts, and persistent security auditing against offending sessions.")
B.ajd=new A.hv("8. Offline-First Architecture, Local Caching, and Synchronization Responsibilities","ClassRealm is constructed upon an offline-first architectural model to guarantee operational continuity even in environments with intermittent or unstable campus internet connectivity:\n\n\u2022 Local Data Caching: Attendance scans, draft grading sheets, and learner progress updates are securely cached in encrypted local database storage on the user's device when offline.\n\u2022 Synchronization Protocol: Cached records are automatically queued and synchronized with the school's central Supabase cloud database as soon as a verified internet connection is re-established.\n\u2022 User Responsibility: Teachers and students are responsible for periodically connecting their mobile devices or laptops to the internet to ensure pending queue items are synchronized. The school cannot be held liable for delayed report generation or missing grade submissions arising from prolonged offline usage without synchronization prior to official deadlines.")
B.ajg=new A.hv("9. Scheduled Maintenance, System Updates, and Emergency Broadcasts","To preserve optimal performance, platform stability, and software security, the school administration reserves the right to perform routine and emergency platform interventions:\n\n\u2022 Maintenance Windows: Scheduled maintenance, database optimizations, and system migrations will be announced in advance through in-app notification banners. Non-administrative users may be temporarily restricted from logging in during active maintenance windows.\n\u2022 Data Preservation: Offline records currently residing on end-user devices remain unaffected and preserved during server maintenance.\n\u2022 Emergency Broadcasts: In cases of severe weather, campus emergencies, or administrative school suspensions, System Administrators may dispatch priority alert banners that override regular notification preferences to ensure immediate campus-wide awareness.")
B.aje=new A.hv("10. Limitation of Liability, Institutional Disclaimer, and Amendments",'ClassRealm is provided to students, parents, and educators on an "as-is" and "as-available" basis for academic pilot deployment, institutional evaluation, and operational school management:\n\n\u2022 Liability Disclaimer: To the fullest extent permitted by Philippine law, Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School, its administrators, faculty members, and the ClassRealm Capstone Development Team shall not be held liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages resulting from lost internet access, device incompatibilities, user failure to safeguard credentials, or unapproved third-party hardware usage.\n\u2022 Amendments: The school administration reserves the right to modify, refine, or update these Terms of Service periodically to reflect evolving Department of Education directives, statutory legal revisions, or institutional school policies. Continued use of the System after amendments are published constitutes full acceptance of the revised Terms.')
